            <ArticleTitle>Lethal coronary air embolism caused by the removal of a double-lumen hemodialysis catheter: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>296-300</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4097/kjae.2016.69.3.296</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary air embolism is a rare event. We report a case in which an acute myocardial infarction occurred in the region supplied by the right coronary artery after the removal of a double-lumen hemodialysis catheter. Emergent coronary angiography revealed air bubbles obstructing the mid-segment of the right coronary artery with slow flow phenomenon distally. The patient expired due to myocardial infarction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
